```text
RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE

Office of City Clerk

February 22, 2019

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date
beginning at 6:07 p.m. in City Council Chambers for the purpose of collective labor bargaining
with the Cheyenne Professional Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local
No. 279.  Present were:  MAYOR - Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Rocky Case, Bryan
Cook, Scott Roybal, Dicky Shanor and Jeff White.  Absent:  Mike Luna, Dr. Mark Rinne, Ken
Esquibel, and Pete Laybourn.  Also present: Kris Jones, City Clerk; Sylvia Hackl, City Attorney;
and Chief Greg Hoggatt, Fire and Rescue Department.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded and available on Facebook live
and stated that Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings Act allows the
governing body to meet in executive session to consider or tender offers regarding salaries, wages
or other terms and conditions of employment during negotiations with the fire fighters union and
that any motion approved by the governing body to move into executive session during the special
meetings would be pursuant to this section of statute.  Mayor Orr further advised if the governing
body met in executive session, they would be meeting in the Mayor’s Conference Room, and that
Fire Union representatives were welcome to use Room 104 for the purpose of meeting to caucus.

Mr. Case moved to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.  Mayor Orr identified, in addition to
members of the governing body present, the City Clerk, City Attorney, and Chief of the Fire and
Rescue Department would also be present at the executive session.  [City Clerk note: Audio
recording of the special meeting was stopped; executive session convened at 6:14 p.m. in the
Mayor’s Conference Room]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at
6:44 p.m.  Mayor Orr noted that spokespersons for the City during negotiations would be Mayor
Orr and Council President Rocky Case and Council Vice-President Bryan Cook.  Additional
members of the negotiation team for the City are Council members Ken Esquibel, Pete Laybourn,
Dr. Mark Rinne, Mike Luna, Greg Hoggatt, Chief, Cheyenne Fire & Rescue, Sylvia Hackl, City
Attorney, Alessandra McCoy Fakelman, Assistant City Attorney, Ron Downey, City
Treasurer/Human Resources and Robyn Lockman, City Treasury.   Union spokespersons would
be Bill Hinz President, and Brandon Braisted, Vice-President, and additional members of the
negotiation team for the Union are Neil Durante, Dan Culter, TJ Haws, Derrick Pollnow, Ryan
Anderson, Dave Evans, and Tom Bauscher.  Mayor Orr confirmed that any agreement reached
between the City and the Union must be approved by the governing body with the agreement
placed on a regular City Council meeting agenda and approved through the Council’s usual
procedures.
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Council President Mr. Case announced that all meetings will be from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM
unless both sides vote to extend for an additional time.

The proposed Ground Rules were submitted by the City to Union spokespersons and Mr.
Hinz advised the Union would like to change Section 2 of the Ground Rules to allow for seven (7)
members on the negotiation team instead of six (6) and the change was verbally acknowledged by
spokespersons representing the City and the Union.  Following signing of the Ground Rules by
Mr. Hinz and Mayor Orr, Mr. Hinz presented the Mayor with the Union’s proposed Collective
Bargaining Agreement.

Mayor Orr announced 2 additional meetings have been scheduled for Wednesday,
February 27, 2019 and Thursday, February 28, 2019 at 6:00 PM to be held in Council Chambers.

Mayor Orr stated the purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no
business previously noted for the special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 6:52 p.m.

Submitted by,

Kristina F. Jones,

City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.

Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

February 28, 2019
```
